Dr. Richard E. Hawkins wrote:
> I'm used to being able to build ports step by step (extract, patch, all,
> install) with FreeBSD; I haven't found intermediate commands (but I
> think I've figured out how to pass environment variables.

Intermediate commands are:
ebuild filename unpack [compile install qmerge]

To unpack NetHack you would use this magic incantation:

cd /usr/portage/app-games/nethack
ebuild nethack-3.4.1-r1.ebuild unpack

After that, NetHack source tree can be found from:
/var/tmp/portage/nethack-3.4.1-r1/work/nethack-3.4.1/

See "man ebuild" for detailed explanation. If paths mentioned above
doesn't seem to work, see /etc/make.conf and /etc/make.globals
for the correct paths.

> Anyway, does anyon know the whole magic for making an X-less nethack
> under gentoo?  

export USE="-X"
emerge nethack

Other possible USE flags are "Qt" and "gnome". ([S] has also "gtk")

> Either that, or the environment variables needed to force this?  

export HACKOPTIONS="windowtype:tty"

Or put that option in your ~/.nethackrc


